{"In CredentialsProvider.authorize(), password verification runs only when credentials.totpCode is absent; providing any non-empty totpCode skips password verification. Because backupCode validation is a separate branch, an attacker can authenticate for a CAL user using only a valid backup code by also sending any totpCode value, resulting in passwordless login": 0.3566809594631195, "PasswordField's show/hide password button is removed from the tab order via tabIndex={-1}, making the visibility toggle inaccessible to keyboard-only users": 0.918014407157898}